{"id":"oncology","cards":[{"id":"oncolo810b20dd","l":1,"f":"<b>Neoplasia</b>?","b":"new tissue growth that is <b>unregulated, irreversible, and monoclonal</b> — these features distinguish it from hyperplasia and repair.","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo5918a85e","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperplasia</b>?","b":"increased number of cells.","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo0aaa82f0","l":1,"f":"<b>Hypertrophy</b>?","b":"increased cell size.","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo7e7e4fa8","l":1,"f":"<b>Metaplasia</b>?","b":"replacement of one differentiated cell type by another.","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo4335cdbc","l":1,"f":"<b>Dysplasia</b>?","b":"abnormal cellular growth and maturation.","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncoloe59d53e1","l":1,"f":"<b>Hypertrophy</b> — Doctor&#x27;s key point?","b":"↑ cell size, no change in number — e.g. cardiac hypertrophy in chronic hypertension","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo71bd4ca9","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperplasia</b> — Doctor&#x27;s key point?","b":"↑ cell number by a regulated stimulus (estrogen/androgen) — <b>regulated and reversible</b> once the stimulus is removed, unlike neoplasia","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo14f5ee67","l":1,"f":"<b>Neoplasia</b> — Doctor&#x27;s key point?","b":"Unregulated, irreversible; usually monoclonal — one mutated cell accumulates more mutations over years","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolobb13f9ec","l":1,"f":"<b>Metaplasia</b> — Doctor&#x27;s key point?","b":"e.g. <b>Barrett esophagus</b>: squamous → columnar (chronic acid reflux)","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo05f6b146","l":1,"f":"<b>Dysplasia</b> — Doctor&#x27;s key point?","b":"Disordered proliferation with atypia (pleomorphism); end result of persistent metaplasia; premalignant if the stimulus persists","c":"Basic terminology"},{"id":"oncolo94e38850","l":1,"f":"<b>Neoplasm ≠ cancer</b>?","b":"a neoplasm may be benign or malignant (e.g. lipoma = benign neoplasm with essentially no invasion/metastasis).","c":"Basic terminology › Neoplasia progression"},{"id":"oncolo45132788","l":1,"f":"<b>Carcinoma in situ</b>?","b":"full-thickness dysplasia that stays <b>above the basement membrane</b>; <b>invasive carcinoma</b> = malignant cells breach the basement membrane.","c":"Basic terminology › Neoplasia progression"},{"id":"oncolocab251b6","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Differentiation?","b":"Usually well differentiated","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolocc4af500","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Differentiation?","b":"Variable / poorly differentiated","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo4f6dcd45","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Growth?","b":"Usually slow","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo8c0c458b","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Growth?","b":"Often faster","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncoloce86a810","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Local invasion?","b":"No","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncoloe2c5c2de","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Local invasion?","b":"Yes","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolob7ab2bb8","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Metastasis?","b":"No","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolob57d3fc2","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Metastasis?","b":"Possible","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo217e1c3e","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Recurrence?","b":"Usually uncommon","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo30c4c7ce","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Recurrence?","b":"May occur","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo579d0b06","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Clinical impact?","b":"Usually local","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo30b5f349","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignant</b> — Clinical impact?","b":"Local + systemic","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolo85b3e160","l":1,"f":"<b>Well differentiated</b>?","b":"closely resembles the tissue of origin, better prognosis","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncoloa65e00d8","l":1,"f":"<b>Poorly differentiated</b>?","b":"minimal resemblance; special stains may be needed","c":"Benign vs malignant"},{"id":"oncolod229aa73","l":1,"f":"<b>Inherited genetic</b> — Examples?","b":"BRCA1/BRCA2 mutations; APC mutation (FAP)","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncoloa55b32f3","l":1,"f":"<b>Inherited genetic</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Breast/ovarian cancer; colorectal cancer","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo2a9aa88d","l":1,"f":"<b>Diet</b> — Examples?","b":"High intake of processed/red meat; smoked and preserved foods","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolod57472f5","l":1,"f":"<b>Diet</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Colorectal cancer; gastric cancer","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolodefe9980","l":1,"f":"<b>Residential environment</b> — Examples?","b":"Radon exposure in homes","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo8a604349","l":1,"f":"<b>Residential environment</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Lung cancer","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo0bb6763a","l":1,"f":"<b>Work environment</b> — Examples?","b":"Asbestos; aromatic amines in dye/rubber industries","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo6e582e09","l":1,"f":"<b>Work environment</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Mesothelioma/lung cancer; bladder cancer","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo85dc7762","l":1,"f":"<b>Lifestyle</b> — Examples?","b":"Smoking; alcohol","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo79baeace","l":1,"f":"<b>Lifestyle</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Lung and many other cancers; liver, upper GI","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo1fc18756","l":1,"f":"<b>Ionising radiation</b> — Examples?","b":"Previous radiotherapy; high environmental radiation","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncoloca4ef359","l":1,"f":"<b>Ionising radiation</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Leukemia, thyroid cancer, various solid tumors","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo7559cab5","l":1,"f":"<b>Carcinogens</b> — Examples?","b":"Aflatoxin B1; benzene","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo2f51ab66","l":1,"f":"<b>Carcinogens</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Hepatocellular carcinoma; leukemia","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo855b487e","l":1,"f":"<b>Viral infection</b> — Examples?","b":"HPV; HBV/HCV","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo88a73957","l":1,"f":"<b>Viral infection</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Cervical/anal/oropharyngeal; hepatocellular carcinoma","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo967dee8b","l":1,"f":"<b>Hormonal</b> — Examples?","b":"Prolonged estrogen; androgen signalling","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo460eabbd","l":1,"f":"<b>Hormonal</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Endometrial/breast; prostate","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo8f849c6f","l":1,"f":"<b>Increasing age</b> — Examples?","b":"Accumulation of somatic mutations","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo02247074","l":1,"f":"<b>Increasing age</b> — Associated malignancy?","b":"Most cancers (colorectal, prostate, pancreatic)","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo302c01e0","l":1,"f":"<b>APC mutation</b>?","b":"earliest event in the adenoma–carcinoma sequence.","c":"Carcinogenesis"},{"id":"oncolo0b9b2238","l":1,"f":"<b>Germline</b>?","b":"inherited/heritable predisposition present throughout the body.","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo0c523fd5","l":1,"f":"<b>Somatic</b>?","b":"acquired mutation arising in particular cells during life.","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolocf1b29bd","l":1,"f":"<b>Somatic</b> — Location?","b":"Only in tumor cells","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo01f1b5a7","l":1,"f":"<b>Germline</b> — Location?","b":"Throughout the body's normal cells","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolof3816ac6","l":1,"f":"<b>Somatic</b> — Inherited??","b":"Not necessarily","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo2f97af49","l":1,"f":"<b>Germline</b> — Inherited??","b":"Yes — hereditary predisposition","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo490a704b","l":1,"f":"<b>Somatic</b> — Testing?","b":"Tumor tissue (guides targeted therapy)","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncoloa218e27a","l":1,"f":"<b>Germline</b> — Testing?","b":"Blood or normal tissue","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolob32f8e8a","l":1,"f":"<b>Somatic</b> — Implication?","b":"Treatment selection","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncoloa8ebd0a6","l":1,"f":"<b>Germline</b> — Implication?","b":"↑ risk of multiple different cancers","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncoloe23dc2b8","l":1,"f":"<b>FAP</b>?","b":"APC mutation + family history → germline testing; predisposes to colorectal and other tumors (small bowel, thyroid).","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolof20d90e1","l":1,"f":"<b>Lynch syndrome</b>?","b":"microsatellite instability (MSI)/MMR deficiency; colorectal + extracolonic cancers (ovarian, pancreatic). Germline. Family history may be absent — a <b>young patient with colorectal cancer</b> should raise suspicion. New CRCs get routine MSI/MMR testing → abnormal → germline testing.","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo57f70fb0","l":1,"f":"<b>DNA mismatch repair</b>?","b":"MMR proteins repair daily replication errors; deficiency → mutations accumulate → genomic instability → cancer.","c":"Genetic mutations"},{"id":"oncolo99fb39f9","l":2,"f":"Average-risk colorectal screening (no family history)","b":"<b>colonoscopy every 10 years starting at 45–50</b>","c":"Prevention › Screening"},{"id":"oncolo85624d7f","l":2,"f":"<b>Lung cancer screening</b>","b":"<b>annual low-dose CT</b> for age <b>50–80</b> with <b>≥ 20 pack-years</b> who smoke now or quit within 15 years: e.g. a 52-year-old, 30 pack-years, quit 10 years ago ; the only candidate among the choices was the <b>51-year-old with 30 pack-years</b> (others too young or too few pack-years)","c":"Prevention › Screening"},{"id":"oncolo5a342d0f","l":1,"f":"<b>High-risk rule</b>?","b":"first-degree relative with CRC at 40 → start colonoscopy at ~30 (10 years earlier than the relative).","c":"Prevention › Screening"},{"id":"oncoloc8df084e","l":2,"f":"70-year-old with <b>bright red blood mixed with stool, weight loss, constipation, pallor</b>","b":"<b>colon cancer (adenocarcinoma)</b>","c":"Diagnosis"},{"id":"oncolo9cad3e5d","l":2,"f":"62-year-old with hematochezia and 3rd-degree hemorrhoids","b":"<b>colonoscopy first</b> (rule out cancer before treating the hemorrhoids)","c":"Diagnosis"},{"id":"oncolo6d6183a2","l":1,"f":"<b>Virchow node (left supraclavicular)</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Classically gastric/intra-abdominal malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo5a65c9ba","l":1,"f":"<b>Sister Mary Joseph nodule (umbilical deposit)</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Intra-abdominal/pelvic malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolof8b4ccc3","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatomegaly / hard nodular liver</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Liver metastases","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo86c8d9b7","l":1,"f":"<b>Ascites</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Peritoneal carcinomatosis, ovarian/GI malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo18eef047","l":1,"f":"<b>Courvoisier sign</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Pancreatic head or periampullary malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolofe77de9f","l":1,"f":"<b>Palpable rectal mass on DRE</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Rectal cancer","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncoloc68b640f","l":1,"f":"<b>Hard irregular breast mass</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Suspicious for breast malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolobc6a8311","l":1,"f":"<b>Fixed/matted lymph nodes</b> — Possible significance?","b":"Metastatic malignancy or lymphoma","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncoloe79a5d1b","l":1,"f":"<b>Tumor marker CEA</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Colorectal cancer — best for follow-up/surveillance of recurrence","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncoloe3b95ae8","l":1,"f":"<b>CA 19-9</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Pancreatic and biliary cancers","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolod341aa29","l":1,"f":"<b>CA-125</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Epithelial ovarian cancer","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolobe3c8b58","l":1,"f":"<b>Tumor marker AFP</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Hepatocellular carcinoma","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo2814bc36","l":1,"f":"<b>Tumor marker PSA</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Prostate cancer","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo6bcbeb79","l":1,"f":"<b>Calcitonin</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Medullary thyroid carcinoma","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo7e1f0429","l":1,"f":"<b>Thyroglobulin</b> — Common cancer association?","b":"Differentiated thyroid cancer","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo20e1d04f","l":2,"f":"Pancreatic head tumor","b":"<b>CA 19-9</b>","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolo9499b287","l":2,"f":"Palpable gallbladder (Courvoisier)","b":"<b>tumor of the head of the pancreas</b>, not a CBD stone","c":"Diagnosis › Clinical findings & tumor markers"},{"id":"oncolob2a24cae","l":1,"f":"<b>Sequence rule</b>?","b":"do not stage before confirming the diagnosis: suspicious lesion → imaging → <b>biopsy</b> → confirm malignancy → staging.","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo70d6cccc","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 0</b> — Meaning?","b":"Incomplete → additional imaging","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolof8ba5938","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 1</b> — Meaning?","b":"Negative","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo124bec69","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 2</b> — Meaning?","b":"Benign","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo40a36f50","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 3</b> — Meaning?","b":"Probably benign → short-interval follow-up","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo5285066f","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 4</b> — Meaning?","b":"Suspicious","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo0ba6e9c8","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 5</b> — Meaning?","b":"Highly suggestive of malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolo56778272","l":1,"f":"<b>BI-RADS 6</b> — Meaning?","b":"Biopsy-proven malignancy","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncolod24c311f","l":2,"f":"Thyroid nodule on exam/US","b":"next step <b>FNA</b>","c":"Diagnosis › Imaging & endoscopy"},{"id":"oncoloeb30ab73","l":1,"f":"<b>FNA</b> — What is obtained??","b":"Cells","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo37646a0c","l":1,"f":"<b>Core biopsy</b> — What is obtained??","b":"Core of tissue","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo192f6071","l":1,"f":"<b>Incisional</b> — What is obtained??","b":"Part of lesion","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo5173ed05","l":1,"f":"<b>Excisional</b> — What is obtained??","b":"Entire lesion","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncoloa4b87539","l":1,"f":"<b>FNA</b> — Tissue architecture?","b":"Limited","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo5468f10a","l":1,"f":"<b>Core biopsy</b> — Tissue architecture?","b":"Yes","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo78e59fe8","l":1,"f":"<b>Incisional</b> — Tissue architecture?","b":"Yes","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo263252b2","l":1,"f":"<b>Excisional</b> — Tissue architecture?","b":"Yes","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncoloefcc3f45","l":1,"f":"<b>FNA</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Lowest","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolod8a5d02b","l":1,"f":"<b>Core biopsy</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Low","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo5f76ffaa","l":1,"f":"<b>Incisional</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Higher","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncoloba89f49b","l":1,"f":"<b>Excisional</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Higher","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolodcd81ccf","l":1,"f":"<b>FNA</b> — Typical example?","b":"Thyroid nodule","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolofe721209","l":1,"f":"<b>Core biopsy</b> — Typical example?","b":"Breast mass","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo2fe98520","l":1,"f":"<b>Incisional</b> — Typical example?","b":"Large lesion when core is unsuitable","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolobc26f115","l":1,"f":"<b>Excisional</b> — Typical example?","b":"Lymph node","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncoloe9d26842","l":1,"f":"<b>FNA</b> — Definitive treatment??","b":"No","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo6d715608","l":1,"f":"<b>Core biopsy</b> — Definitive treatment??","b":"No","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncoloebd1c9c6","l":1,"f":"<b>Incisional</b> — Definitive treatment??","b":"No","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo78721a17","l":1,"f":"<b>Excisional</b> — Definitive treatment??","b":"Sometimes","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo1d4b8ec5","l":1,"f":"<b>Myth</b>?","b":"biopsy routinely spreading cancer is incorrect.","c":"Diagnosis › Biopsy"},{"id":"oncolo538ba864","l":1,"f":"<b>IHC</b>?","b":"antibodies detect specific proteins. Purposes: tumor type → cytokeratin (carcinoma), CD45 (lymphoma); primary origin → CDX2/SATB2 (colorectal), PAX8 (renal/Müllerian); guide treatment → ER/PR/HER2; proliferation → Ki-67; molecular pathway → MMR proteins (MLH1, PMS2, MSH2, MSH6); sarcoma → CD117/DOG1 (GIST).","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo96d2a72a","l":1,"f":"<b>IHC marker CK7</b> — Association / use?","b":"Breast, lung, ovarian, pancreatobiliary, urothelial","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo5db2c192","l":1,"f":"<b>CK20</b> — Association / use?","b":"Colorectal and urothelial","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo4a9d3416","l":1,"f":"<b>CDX2</b> — Association / use?","b":"Intestinal/colorectal","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo6db57816","l":1,"f":"<b>SATB2</b> — Association / use?","b":"Colorectal/appendiceal","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo36256a77","l":1,"f":"<b>TTF-1</b> — Association / use?","b":"Lung adenocarcinoma and thyroid","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo9734c5ba","l":1,"f":"<b>PAX8</b> — Association / use?","b":"Renal, thyroid, Müllerian","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo4731a274","l":1,"f":"<b>ER/PR</b> — Association / use?","b":"Breast &amp; gynecologic; predict hormonal therapy","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo2e07b9c4","l":1,"f":"<b>HER2</b> — Association / use?","b":"Breast, selected gastric/GEJ; predict targeted therapy","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolof9d9c6a9","l":1,"f":"<b>PSA/NKX3.1</b> — Association / use?","b":"Prostatic origin","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo37b2a16f","l":1,"f":"<b>Synaptophysin, Chromogranin A</b> — Association / use?","b":"Neuroendocrine","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo762ecbfc","l":1,"f":"<b>S100/SOX10</b> — Association / use?","b":"Melanocytic and neural","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo857f1a5c","l":1,"f":"<b>Melan-A/HMB45</b> — Association / use?","b":"Melanoma","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncoloeca3c471","l":1,"f":"<b>CD117 (KIT)</b> — Association / use?","b":"GIST","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolof2c6f6e1","l":1,"f":"<b>Desmin</b> — Association / use?","b":"Smooth muscle (leiomyosarcoma)","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo8ff9468a","l":1,"f":"<b>Cancer of unknown primary</b>?","b":"metastasis found but primary not seen → biopsy the metastasis (liver/peritoneum) → IHC panel to estimate origin; molecular profiling guides therapy.","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolo748e8dd0","l":2,"f":"Submucosal gastric mass with normal mucosa and central ulceration, presenting with hematemesis","b":"<b>GIST</b> (CD117)","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncoloc9f2cc69","l":2,"f":"Hashimoto's thyroiditis + rapidly enlarging diffuse goitre","b":"<b>thyroid lymphoma</b>","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolob0713882","l":2,"f":"Diagnostic pre-treatment tumor marker in thyroid cancer (keyed)","b":"<b>calcitonin</b> (medullary); thyroglobulin is for <b>follow-up after total thyroidectomy</b> in differentiated cancer","c":"Diagnosis › Histopathology & IHC"},{"id":"oncolocd430f01","l":2,"f":"Colon (splenic-flexure) adenocarcinoma","b":"staging by <b>CT chest, abdomen and pelvis</b>","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo83922a5d","l":2,"f":"Biopsy-proven gastric adenocarcinoma","b":"next step <b>CT scan</b> (staging) — EUS and diagnostic laparoscopy come after","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo5ddebd6c","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage T1</b> — Rectal cancer — extent of invasion?","b":"Submucosa","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo1a7c9ec8","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage T2</b> — Rectal cancer — extent of invasion?","b":"Muscularis propria","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo13343fe4","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage T3</b> — Rectal cancer — extent of invasion?","b":"Beyond muscularis propria into mesorectal/perirectal tissue (depth matters)","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo42a1483d","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage T4a</b> — Rectal cancer — extent of invasion?","b":"Penetrates the visceral peritoneal surface","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo571d4d08","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage T4b</b> — Rectal cancer — extent of invasion?","b":"Directly invades adjacent organs","c":"Staging"},{"id":"oncolo1b5104ce","l":1,"f":"<b>Colorectal</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Liver, lung, peritoneum","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo12559fb8","l":1,"f":"<b>Colorectal</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Liver most characteristic (portal circulation)","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncoloc53a16ed","l":1,"f":"<b>Rectal</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Liver, lung, peritoneum","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo683e0d28","l":1,"f":"<b>Rectal</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Distal rectum can spread to lung <b>without</b> passing through the liver","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolob02b6ec8","l":1,"f":"<b>Pancreatic</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Liver, peritoneum, lung","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo731f936d","l":1,"f":"<b>Pancreatic</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Liver metastases common","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolobc19f824","l":1,"f":"<b>Gastric</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Liver, peritoneum, distant nodes, ovary","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo2811601f","l":1,"f":"<b>Gastric</b> — High-yield point?","b":"<b>Krukenberg</b> tumor; <b>Virchow</b> node","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncoloa3652219","l":1,"f":"<b>Esophageal</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Liver, lung, bone","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo9b6b439f","l":1,"f":"<b>Esophageal</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Extensive lymphatic spread","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo274fc81b","l":1,"f":"<b>Breast</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Bone, lung, liver, brain","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo4a22d4d8","l":1,"f":"<b>Breast</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Bone very common","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncoloa8fb45e0","l":1,"f":"<b>Prostate</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Bone","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo8630cc46","l":1,"f":"<b>Prostate</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Osteoblastic, axial skeleton","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo1eb32f19","l":1,"f":"<b>Lung</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Brain, bone, liver, adrenal","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolocc0a1df8","l":1,"f":"<b>Lung</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Brain/adrenal classic","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolob193276f","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal cell</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Lung, bone, liver, brain","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo25be23c3","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal cell</b> — High-yield point?","b":"\"Cannonball\" lung metastases","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolodefe924b","l":1,"f":"<b>Ovarian</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Peritoneum/omentum, pleura","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo08d903b4","l":1,"f":"<b>Ovarian</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Transcoelomic","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncoloc0ff15c9","l":1,"f":"<b>Sarcoma</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Lung","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo933a9868","l":1,"f":"<b>Sarcoma</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Hematogenous","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolob5882f91","l":1,"f":"<b>Testicular</b> — Common metastatic sites?","b":"Retroperitoneal nodes, lung","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo42fcf59e","l":1,"f":"<b>Testicular</b> — High-yield point?","b":"Follows gonadal drainage","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo1ca85ec6","l":1,"f":"<b>Clinical pearl</b>?","b":"male with a <b>retroperitoneal mass → examine the testes</b>.","c":"Staging › Routes of spread & common metastatic sites"},{"id":"oncolo4e54e697","l":1,"f":"<b>Resectability</b>?","b":"can the tumor technically and oncologically be completely removed?","c":"MDT: resectability & operability"},{"id":"oncoloa4eeac96","l":1,"f":"<b>Operability</b>?","b":"fitness for surgery — can the patient safely tolerate the operation?","c":"MDT: resectability & operability"},{"id":"oncolo81a5dfde","l":1,"f":"<b>En bloc</b>?","b":"tumor + directly involved adjacent organ(s) removed together without cutting through the tumor plane (e.g. colon cancer invading bladder/uterus → resect with the colon).","c":"Surgical management › Curative surgery"},{"id":"oncolocc18f240","l":2,"f":"Obstructing rectosigmoid/low rectal cancer <b>with liver and lung metastases</b>","b":"<b>diverting stoma (transverse colostomy)</b>","c":"Surgical management › Palliative surgery"},{"id":"oncolo2add3ff5","l":1,"f":"<b>Neoadjuvant</b>?","b":"before definitive surgery","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolo71199863","l":1,"f":"<b>Adjuvant</b>?","b":"after surgery","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncoloc277b8f8","l":1,"f":"<b>Perioperative</b>?","b":"before and/or after","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolo1a4f1de9","l":1,"f":"<b>Definitive</b>?","b":"primary curative modality","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolod97be0f4","l":1,"f":"<b>Palliative</b>?","b":"symptom control/prolonging life","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncoloa28df5d0","l":1,"f":"<b>Melanoma</b>?","b":"immunotherapy can produce major/complete responses.","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolodd703d21","l":1,"f":"<b>Rectal cancer — TNT (total neoadjuvant therapy)</b>?","b":"chemo + radiotherapy before surgery → <b>~30–40% complete clinical response</b>, allowing selected patients to avoid immediate resection under close surveillance.","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncoloa54a798b","l":2,"f":"Locally advanced low rectal cancer (T3N1M0), not obstructed","b":"<b>start with (chemo)radiation</b> (neoadjuvant), not upfront surgery","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolofc4a9f7d","l":2,"f":"Neoadjuvant radiotherapy role in rectal cancer","b":"<b>down-stage the tumor</b> ; neoadjuvant radiotherapy = <b>local control</b>","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncolo9b490437","l":2,"f":"HCC on cirrhosis within Milan criteria (single ≤5 cm, Child B)","b":"<b>liver transplant</b>","c":"Multimodal treatment"},{"id":"oncoloc125d6e4","l":1,"f":"<b>Colorectal</b>?","b":"~95% of recurrences within 2 years, nearly all by ~3 years; intensive surveillance largely finished by 5 years.","c":"Surveillance"},{"id":"oncolobc72fb41","l":2,"f":"\"When is she cured?\"","b":"<b>a normal duration of life without further clinical or radiological evidence</b> of cancer","c":"Surveillance"},{"id":"oncolodb2330f4","l":2,"f":"<b>Marjolin ulcer</b>","b":"<b>SCC</b> arising in a chronic scar/burn","c":"Other organ facts asked under oncology"},{"id":"oncoloc90bf27b","l":2,"f":"Picture of an ulcerated skin lesion","b":"<b>SCC</b>","c":"Other organ facts asked under oncology"}]}